## 2. ISA specification
### 2.1 Encoding (R-type, opcode = `CUSTOM1` = `0x2B`)
```
31 25 24 20 19 15 14 12 11 7 6 0
+-----------+-------+-------+------+------+---------+
| funct7 | rs2 | rs1 |funct3| rd | opcode |
+-----------+-------+-------+------+------+---------+
9 | ldm | base | ES T| fd | CUSTOM1 ← vx.ldm
10 | ldm | base | ES T| fs | CUSTOM1 ← vx.stm
```
| Field | Width | Meaning |
|---------|-------|---------|
| `funct7`| 7 | **9** = load, **10** = store |
| `rs1` | 5 | integer register holding tile base pointer (uniform across
warp) |
| `rs2` | 5 | integer register holding `ldm` (leading dimension, in
*elements*; uniform) |
| `rd` / `fs` | 5 | starting FP register of the 8-register fragment (f0…f31) |
| `funct3[0]` | 1 | `T` — transpose (0 = row-major, 1 = col-major) |
| `funct3[2:1]` | 2 | `ES` — element size: 00=8b, 01=16b, 10=32b, 11=64b |
`NR` (registers per fragment) is hardwired to **8**.
### 2.2 Fragment register ABI
The starting register `rd` selects the fragment bank (matches the `mma_sync` ABI):
| `rd` | Fragment | Notes |
|------|----------|-------|
| `0` | `matrix_a` | f0–f7 |
| `10` | `matrix_b` | f10–f17 (used only when NRB=8) |
| `24` | `accumulator` | f24–f31 |
Role (A / B / C) is **derived** from `rd[4:0]` at the AGU call site — no explicit
role field in the instruction.
### 2.3 Blocked address formula
For lane `L`, uop counter `r`, and role:
```
┌ lane-origin ───────────────┐ ┌ register step ───────────────┐
matrix_a: row = L/tcK + block_idx*tcM + (r/k_steps) * (a_sub_blocks*tcM)
col = (L%tcK)*i_ratio + (r%k_steps) * (tcK*i_ratio)
matrix_b: row = (L%tcK)*i_ratio + (r/b_sub_steps) * (tcK*i_ratio)
col = L/tcK + block_idx*tcN + (r%b_sub_steps) * (b_sub_blocks*tcN)
accumulator: row = L/tcN + (r/n_steps)*tcM
col = L%tcN + (r%n_steps)*tcN
if T: swap(row, col)
addr = base + (row * ldm + col) * (1 << ES)
```
Tile constants (`tcM`, `tcN`, `tcK`, `i_ratio`, `*_steps`, `*_sub_blocks`) come
from `wmma_config_t<NT>` in [sim/common/tensor_cfg.h](sim/common/tensor_cfg.h); the
RTL AGU duplicates them as localparams so the extension is available without TCU.
### 2.4 Microarchitecture: macro → uop split + LSU AGU
Each `vx.ldm` / `vx.stm` macro instruction is **expanded into 8 LSU uops** (one per
fragment register) by the uop sequencer. The per-lane blocked address is computed
by the **LSU AGU** inside the LSU slice:
```
decode uop sequencer operand fetch dispatch → LSU slice
+--------+ +---------------+ +------------+ +---------+ +---------+
| MLD/ | ---> | VX_lsu_uops | --> | r0/r1/r2 | -> | buffer |->| AGU + |
| MST | | 8 uops | | fetched | | | | LSU ops |
| macro | | stamp r, | | | | | +---------+
| | | inc rd/rs2 | | | | |
+--------+ +---------------+ +------------+ +---------+
op_args.ldm op_args.ldm{r=0..7} rs1/rs2/rs3_data
(es, t, r=0)
```
**Two distinct args types** reflect the two-tier design:
- **`ldm_args_t`** (macro): `{ es, t, r }` — what decode extracts from the ISA.
Fits in the `op_args` union alongside `alu_args_t`, `lsu_args_t`, etc.
- **`lsu_args_t`** (uop): `{ width, is_float, offset, is_store }` — plain LSU
plumbing; matrix ops piggyback on the LSU datapath but their op_type (`MLD`/`MST`)
makes the AGU take over address computation.
The decoder emits `op_args.ldm`; the sequencer stamps `r` per uop; the LSU slice's
AGU consumes `op_args.ldm.{es, t, r}` + role-derived-from-`rd[4:0]` to compute the
per-lane address.
