## 3. Part A — SimX implementation (2.5 pts)
### Step A1. Type system
**File:** `sim/simx/types.h` *(provided complete — no changes needed)*
The type system extensions are already provided:
```cpp
enum class LsuType {
LOAD, STORE, FENCE,
MLD, // vx.ldm — matrix LSU load (always available)
MST, // vx.stm — matrix LSU store (always available)
};
struct IntrLdmArgs {
uint32_t es : 2; // element-size log2
uint32_t t : 1; // transpose
uint32_t r : 3; // uop counter 0..7
};
```
`IntrLdmArgs` is already added to the `IntrArgs` variant. Familiarize yourself with
these types before proceeding.
### Step A2. Decode `CUSTOM1` into 8 LSU uops
**File:** `sim/simx/decode.cpp`
Add a `case Opcode::EXT2:` handler. Parse `es` and `t` from `funct3`, determine
whether it is a load or store from `funct7`, and expand the single macro into 8
uops (one per fragment register `r = 0..7`). For each uop, set the opcode type
(`MLD` or `MST`), fill `IntrLdmArgs{es, t, r}`, assign the correct source and
destination registers, and push the instruction to the ibuffer.
The boilerplate for uuid stamping and the loop are provided — your task is to fill
in the instruction fields inside the loop:
```cpp
case Opcode::EXT2: {
// Matrix LSU extension:
// CUSTOM1 (0x2B), vx.ldm (funct7=9), vx.stm (funct7=10).
// Each instruction expands into 8 LSU uops with LsuType::MLD or MST:
// MLD uop: Integer rs1=base, Integer rs2=ldm, Float dest=reg0+r
// MST uop: Integer rs1=base, Float rs2=reg0+r, Integer rs3=ldm
// The per-uop IntrLdmArgs carries es, t, and the counter r.
if (funct7 != 9 && funct7 != 10) std::abort();
uint32_t uuid_hi = (uuid >> 32) & 0xffffffff;
uint32_t uuid_lo = uuid & 0xffffffff;
uint32_t uuid_shift = 32 - 3; // top 3 bits carry r
for (uint32_t r = 0; r < 8; ++r) {
uint32_t uuid_lo_x = (r << uuid_shift) | uuid_lo;
uint64_t uuid_x = (static_cast<uint64_t>(uuid_hi) << 32) | uuid_lo_x;
auto instr = std::allocate_shared<Instr>(instr_pool_, uuid_x, FUType::LSU);
// TODO: set instruction opcode type, destination, source registers, args.
ibuffer.push_back(instr);
}
} break;
```
