## 5. Reference speedup (measured)
| Simulator | Dims | Baseline instrs | `vx.ldm/stm` instrs | Instr ↓ | Baseline
cycles | `vx.ldm/stm` cycles | Cycle Δ |
|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| SimX | 32×32×32 | 58,869 | 48,036 | **18%** | 42,147 | 39,642 |
**−6%** |
| SimX | 64×64×64 | 401,781 | 317,732 | **21%** | 209,817 | 186,885 |
**−11%** |
| SimX | 128×128×128 | 3,020,661 | 2,357,028 | **22%** | 1,587,396 | 1,371,089 |
**−14%** |
| rtlsim | 32×32×32 | — | 42,062 | — | — | 41,128 |
— |
| rtlsim | 64×64×64 | — | 193,486 | — | — | 90,371 |
— |
**Instruction-count reduction is the headline result (12–22%).** SimX now also
shows cycle savings that scale with tile count (4–14% faster at larger dims)
because the uop-expansion model amortizes well. On rtlsim cycles go up slightly —
the 8 LSU uops per macro currently serialize through the single LSU port; a wider
LSU that issues the tile in parallel would recover this overhead (left as a follow-
on optimization).
